atom	ceremonies_instances	the ceremonies of the Roman Catholic religion may be considered as instances of the same nature
atom	external_enliven	the external motions, postures and actions of the ceremonies enliven devotion and quicken fervour, which otherwise would decay if directed entirely to distant and immaterial objects
atom	types_present	shadowing out the objects of faith in sensible types and images renders them more present than is possible by a merely intellectual view and contemplation
atom	sensible_influence	sensible objects have always a greater influence on the fancy than any other
atom	convey_related	sensible objects readily convey this influence to those ideas to which they are related and which they resemble
atom	resemblance_common	the effect of resemblance in enlivening the ideas is very common
atom	concur	in every case a resemblance and a present impression must concur
atom	principle_proved	we are abundantly supplied with experiments to prove the reality of the foregoing principle
